Describe the twenty domain packages, and guard the graph

The prose still described a four-package chain ending in ProjecturedDomain.

- documentation/domains.md replaces the old domain-package architecture guide:
  what a domain package holds, the dependency table, what is NOT a domain (a
  framework two domains share, a domain-neutral editor feature, the
  render-anything projection — all three live in visual), the root module's
  binding loop, and how to add a domain.
- documentation/architecture.md gets the new package chain, the thirteen visual
  slices, and honest opt-in edges: Sdl, Web, Video and Tulip depend on visual,
  Odbc on Sql, DbCatalog and Database, Adaptagrams on Graph.
- CLAUDE.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, README.md, testing.md, tutorial-new-domain.md and
  the moved per-domain guides follow. The plans are history and stay as written.

New: test_package_graph() reads every package/*/main/Project.toml and asserts
the graph is acyclic, that each domain declares exactly the domain edges the
table allows, that each depends on all three engine packages, and that no
engine package depends on a domain. One package per domain only pays off while
the edges stay honest, and a stray [deps] line is one line that nothing else
would catch. A cycle is reported with the edge that closes it.

Verified: test_package_graph 104 pass; test_export_collisions still clean across
the new packages; test_json and test_workbench green.
